sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor HR as HR Manager
  participant UI as Next.js Frontend
  participant API as FastAPI Backend
  participant Celery as Background Worker
  participant DB as PostgreSQL

  note over HR, DB: 1. Viewing the Analytics Dashboard
  HR->>UI: Logs in & views Dashboard
  UI->>API: GET /api/v1/analytics/summary
  API->>DB: Execute Aggregation Queries (AVG, SUM, COUNT)
  DB-->>API: Return Aggregated Metrics
  API-->>UI: JSON Payload (Metrics data)
  UI-->>HR: Renders beautiful charts and KPIs

  note over HR, DB: 2. Browsing 10,000+ Employees Safely
  HR->>UI: Navigates to Employee Directory
  UI->>API: GET /api/v1/employees?page=1&limit=50&department=Engineering
  API->>DB: Execute Indexed SQL Query with OFFSET/LIMIT
  DB-->>API: Return exactly 50 rows
  API-->>UI: JSON Payload (50 records + Total Count)
  UI-->>HR: Displays fast, responsive data table

  note over HR, DB: 3. Performing a Bulk Salary Update (The Scalable Way)
  HR->>UI: Clicks "Give 5% Raise to Engineering"
  UI->>API: POST /api/v1/salaries/bulk-update (Dept: Engineering, +5%)
  API->>Celery: Enqueue Background Task (Do not block the API!)
  API-->>UI: HTTP 202 Accepted (Returns Task ID)
  UI-->>HR: Displays "Update in progress..." toast notification
  
  Celery->>DB: Execute Heavy Bulk UPDATE SQL
  DB-->>Celery: Commit Transaction
  Celery-->>UI: Task Complete (UI polls or gets WebSocket event)
  UI-->>HR: Displays "Success! Salaries Updated."
